id: saibamen-capsule
name: Saibamen Capsule
kind: gear
# A Special Basic Item: only the ARC hands it out, and nothing crafts it.
special: true
# "When you first gain this Basic Item, roll a 1d8. The Dice Score is the amount of Saibamen
# you possess." Rolled when it is given, shown on its row, editable on the Item.
chargesDice: 1d8
chargesLabel: Saibamen
source: Core Rule
description: >
  1d8 Saibamen Seeds. Planted for an Action, they sprout at the start of the next Combat
  Round as Saibamen Minions.
text: >
  Saibamen Capsule: A container for seeds, these alien plants grow quickly into
  semi-intelligent creatures capable of following basic instructions.
  –Effects: When you first gain this Basic Item, roll a 1d8. The Dice Score is the amount of
  Saibamen you possess. You can spend 1 Action to plant a Saibamen Seed. At the start of the
  next Combat Round, all Saibamen Seeds planted during this Combat Round will sprout on any
  Square within 2 Squares of you (you decide) and turn into a number of Saibamen equal to the
  number of seeds planted.

  Saibamen are Minions made through the Minion Creation Rules and must select Saibamen as their
  race.

---

# The roll, and nothing else, by the table's ruling: 1d8 Saibamen when it is given, the count
# on its row and editable on the Item.
#
# Planting, the sprouting, and the Saibamen themselves are done by hand: each is a Minion made
# through the Minion Creation Rules, which is building a character. The player spends the
# Action and lowers the count; the ARC makes the Saibamen.
